WEBVTT

1
00:02:21.776 --> 00:02:22.777
What are you doing?

2
00:02:24.112 --> 00:02:26.581
Nothing. I thought
I heard Brandon crying.

3
00:02:27.982 --> 00:02:29.684
You going someplace?

4
00:02:31.853 --> 00:02:32.720
No.

5
00:02:32.754 --> 00:02:33.755
No. I'm not.

6
00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:36.456
What's in the bag?

7
00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:41.829
Nothing its just
Brandon's belongings.

8
00:02:43.931 --> 00:02:45.099
It's Brandon's.

9
00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:46.433
What's in the bag.

10
00:02:49.336 --> 00:02:50.872
Please.
It's nothing.

11
00:02:51.405 --> 00:02:52.840
Sam. please.
I--

12
00:02:57.111 --> 00:02:58.880
Please. for me.
Please.

13
00:03:22.537 --> 00:03:23.571
Mrs. Labon.

14
00:03:26.074 --> 00:03:27.842
I was asking
if she has a name yet.

15
00:03:29.577 --> 00:03:30.578
Yes.

16
00:03:31.445 --> 00:03:32.412
Natasha.

17
00:03:34.849 --> 00:03:35.850
She's beautiful.

18
00:03:36.718 --> 00:03:37.719
Thank you.

19
00:03:40.655 --> 00:03:43.791
Do the doctors know
why she was born premature?

20
00:03:46.761 --> 00:03:47.762
Not yet.

21
00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.065
Have you been under any
kind of stress

22
00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:52.299
lately?

23
00:03:54.202 --> 00:03:55.402
Why?

24
00:03:57.105 --> 00:03:59.140
Well. stress and anxiety
can be one

25
00:03:59.173 --> 00:04:01.308
of the causes
of premature birth.

26
00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:03.811
She's a tough girl.

27
00:04:05.546 --> 00:04:07.582
only seven months
in and she's ready to take

28
00:04:07.615 --> 00:04:08.616
on the world.

29
00:04:10.484 --> 00:04:13.253
Or maybe it was
just too painful to stay inside.

30
00:04:17.024 --> 00:04:18.025
You know.

31
00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.229
Albert Einstein. Isaac Newton
and Stevie Wonder

32
00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.697
were all premature babies.

33
00:04:23.698 --> 00:04:25.600
I'd say that's not
a coincidence.

34
00:04:27.135 --> 00:04:28.169
They were all fighting
for their lives

35
00:04:28.202 --> 00:04:29.737
since the day they were born.

36
00:04:33.174 --> 00:04:34.909
You seem like a fighter too.

37
00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:43.851
Did you hear that?

38
00:04:47.088 --> 00:04:50.390
You're a fighter like Mama?

39
00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:15.516
<i>It was 1987. Iranian New Year.</i>

40
00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:20.588
<i>We were celebrating Nowruz</i>
<i>with dates back over 3000 years.</i>

41
00:05:20.621 --> 00:05:24.125
<i>Its purpose is to celebrate</i>
<i>the beginning of Spring.</i>

42
00:05:24.158 --> 00:05:26.561
<i>the renewal of nature.</i>

43
00:05:26.594 --> 00:05:28.963
<i>It symbolized much more</i>
<i>than that.</i>

44
00:05:28.996 --> 00:05:30.965
<i>It was a passing of the torch.</i>

45
00:05:30.998 --> 00:05:33.701
<i>When the older family members</i>
<i>would shower</i>

46
00:05:33.734 --> 00:05:37.038
<i>the young generation</i>
<i>with money and gifts.</i>

47
00:05:38.072 --> 00:05:41.509
<i>All Iranians loved to entertain.</i>

48
00:05:42.276 --> 00:05:44.712
<i>Whenever the doorbell rang.</i>

49
00:05:44.745 --> 00:05:49.217
<i>I ran to see who had arrived.</i>
<i>and in typical Iranian fashion.</i>

50
00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:51.919
<i>welcomed everyone with kisses.</i>

51
00:05:51.953 --> 00:05:56.123
<i>Those years were surrounded</i>
<i>by family at love.</i>

52
00:05:58.826 --> 00:06:01.229
<i>During the reign</i>
<i>of the late Shah of Iran.</i>

53
00:06:01.262 --> 00:06:03.164
<i>many sought change</i>

54
00:06:03.197 --> 00:06:06.634
<i>and believed Islamists</i>
<i>would bring a better life</i>

55
00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:07.935
<i>to the people of Iran.</i>

56
00:06:08.769 --> 00:06:09.904
<i>The revolution</i>

57
00:06:09.937 --> 00:06:11.438
<i>abolished the monarchy</i>

58
00:06:11.973 --> 00:06:13.174
<i>and the Ayatollah.</i>

59
00:06:13.207 --> 00:06:15.877
<i>the religious Muslim</i>
<i>fundamentalists</i>

60
00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:16.944
<i>seized power.</i>

61
00:06:18.279 --> 00:06:21.349
<i>However. the outcome was far</i>
<i>from what people had hoped for.</i>

62
00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:22.683
<i>Violence</i>

63
00:06:22.717 --> 00:06:25.253
<i>and disarray ensued.</i>
<i>and people's freedom</i>

64
00:06:25.286 --> 00:06:28.923
<i>was gradually shipped away.</i>
<i>especially those of women.</i>

65
00:06:29.991 --> 00:06:31.559
<i>My beloved daughter Darya</i>

66
00:06:31.592 --> 00:06:33.561
<i>always wanted</i>
<i>to become a doctor.</i>

67
00:06:33.594 --> 00:06:36.597
<i>She was eight years old</i>
<i>when the bombings of the cities</i>

68
00:06:36.631 --> 00:06:38.666
<i>and civilians intensified.</i>

69
00:06:48.342 --> 00:06:50.945
<i>It was that day.</i>
<i>I decided it was time</i>

70
00:06:50.978 --> 00:06:52.213
<i>for my daughter</i>

71
00:06:52.246 --> 00:06:54.916
<i>to leave Iran for good.</i>

72
00:10:23.357 --> 00:10:24.358
Hello.

73
00:10:25.392 --> 00:10:26.627
Hello.

74
00:10:41.475 --> 00:10:43.244
Take off those headphones.
please.

75
00:10:46.615 --> 00:10:47.882
Headphones off.

76
00:10:48.983 --> 00:10:49.984
Good girl.

77
00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:52.554
It's for your own benefit.

78
00:10:52.587 --> 00:10:54.054
You'll thank me later.

79
00:10:55.723 --> 00:10:57.358
My God. what are you watching?

80
00:10:58.560 --> 00:10:59.528
World War II?

81
00:10:59.561 --> 00:11:00.629
No.

82
00:11:00.661 --> 00:11:02.963
It's Tehran
during the Iran-Iraq War.

83
00:11:03.532 --> 00:11:04.932
Mom. were you there?

84
00:11:05.466 --> 00:11:06.667
Where?

85
00:11:10.539 --> 00:11:11.640
Oh. yes.

86
00:11:11.672 --> 00:11:12.873
Yes. I was.

87
00:11:13.874 --> 00:11:15.042
I lost my best friend there.

88
00:11:15.075 --> 00:11:16.477
actually.

89
00:11:16.511 --> 00:11:18.078
Our school was blown up. too.

90
00:11:19.581 --> 00:11:20.781
She was only 12.

91
00:11:21.248 --> 00:11:22.249
Damn.

92
00:11:22.883 --> 00:11:24.118
How did you get out?

93
00:11:25.052 --> 00:11:27.154
I was one of the lucky ones.
I guess.

94
00:11:27.721 --> 00:11:29.356
It's okay. I'm here.

95
00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:30.457
That's hard to watch.

96
00:11:34.395 --> 00:11:35.396
I got it.

97
00:11:41.936 --> 00:11:42.671
Hi.

98
00:11:42.703 --> 00:11:44.171
Is your mom home?

99
00:11:45.372 --> 00:11:46.207
Mom?

100
00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.241
Yes.

101
00:11:47.274 --> 00:11:48.409
The police are here.

102
00:11:48.842 --> 00:11:50.044
What's going on?

103
00:11:50.612 --> 00:11:51.779
Hi. can I help you?

104
00:11:51.812 --> 00:11:53.047
Darya Labon?

105
00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:55.349
Yes. it's Davoudi now.
my maiden name.

106
00:11:55.382 --> 00:11:59.386
Ms. Davoudi. my name is
Detective Emmanuel Goddard.

107
00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:00.354
LAPD homicide.

108
00:12:00.387 --> 00:12:02.256
This is my partner.
Detective Janet Carter.

109
00:12:02.289 --> 00:12:05.159
May we speak to you in private.
please?

110
00:12:05.192 --> 00:12:05.993
Sure.

111
00:12:06.026 --> 00:12:08.295
Can you go up to your rooms.
please?

112
00:12:08.996 --> 00:12:10.297
-Mom.
-It's okay.

113
00:12:10.331 --> 00:12:11.332
Go ahead.
It's okay.

114
00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:17.271
Please. come in.

115
00:12:20.241 --> 00:12:21.242
Thank you.

116
00:12:25.079 --> 00:12:26.914
Would you like to have a seat?

117
00:12:27.582 --> 00:12:28.849
No. thank you.

118
00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:30.117
Ms. Davoudi.

119
00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:31.819
Gosh. no easy way to say this.

120
00:12:31.852 --> 00:12:32.920
I'm going
to come right out with it.

121
00:12:32.953 --> 00:12:34.255
We believe your life
is in danger

122
00:12:34.288 --> 00:12:36.257
and that someone wants
to harm you.

123
00:12:37.391 --> 00:12:38.759
Harm me?

124
00:12:39.561 --> 00:12:40.528
Who?

125
00:12:40.562 --> 00:12:41.762
Why?

126
00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:45.332
What's your relationship like
with your ex-husband. Sam Labon?

127
00:12:47.602 --> 00:12:48.869
Why are you asking me
about Sam?

128
00:12:48.902 --> 00:12:50.137
Is he okay. or--

129
00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:52.273
When's the last time
you spoke to him?

130
00:12:54.308 --> 00:12:56.944
He actually
just recently helped my father

131
00:12:56.977 --> 00:12:59.079
with something
with his passport.

132
00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.348
What is this about?

133
00:13:02.584 --> 00:13:05.452
Ms. Davoudi. your ex-husband
has put a hit out on your life.

134
00:13:07.454 --> 00:13:08.455
I'm sorry. what?

135
00:13:09.624 --> 00:13:12.226
He made a credible attempt
to hire a hitman to torture

136
00:13:12.259 --> 00:13:13.260
and kill you.

137
00:13:13.494 --> 00:13:14.795
Sam?

138
00:13:14.828 --> 00:13:16.430
No. that's not possible.

139
00:13:16.997 --> 00:13:18.399
I know my ex-husband.

140
00:13:18.432 --> 00:13:20.000
He can be intense at times.
but he would never do anything

141
00:13:20.034 --> 00:13:21.135
like that.
-Is there any reason

142
00:13:21.168 --> 00:13:23.137
why you think he'd want
to do this to you?

143
00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:24.171
No.

144
00:13:24.639 --> 00:13:25.607
No.

145
00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:26.840
I don't know.

146
00:13:28.409 --> 00:13:29.376
Everything is fine.

147
00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:32.012
Our divorce was just finalized
two weeks ago.

148
00:13:32.046 --> 00:13:34.315
and the judge
actually ordered him

149
00:13:34.348 --> 00:13:38.452
to pay me $2.5 million.
but I ended up forgiving that.

150
00:13:38.485 --> 00:13:42.557
I let him keep the property.
and there must be some mistake.

151
00:13:44.058 --> 00:13:45.859
We have something to show you.

152
00:13:45.893 --> 00:13:48.596
I want to warn you.
it won't be easy to watch.

153
00:13:50.397 --> 00:13:52.900
- I want the face.
the legs. the back.

154
00:13:52.933 --> 00:13:54.468
the spine all messed up.

155
00:13:55.102 --> 00:13:57.037
and permanent damage.

156
00:13:57.071 --> 00:13:58.807
I need to know
when it's going to happen.

157
00:13:58.839 --> 00:14:02.376
because I need an alibi. right?

158
00:14:02.409 --> 00:14:06.880
I need her hurt
from her spine to her knees.

159
00:14:06.914 --> 00:14:08.382
You want me to kill her?

160
00:14:08.415 --> 00:14:10.618
If she dies.
I got no problem with that.

161
00:14:16.758 --> 00:14:17.958
Okay.

162
00:14:18.959 --> 00:14:20.762
Can I get you anything.

163
00:14:20.795 --> 00:14:22.363
water. tea. anything?

164
00:14:22.396 --> 00:14:24.298
Ms. Davoudi.

165
00:14:24.331 --> 00:14:25.332
we can help you.

166
00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:27.868
We're going to need to find
some place where you

167
00:14:27.901 --> 00:14:29.804
and your children can stay.

168
00:14:29.838 --> 00:14:31.305
Oh. no. I'm not leaving.

169
00:14:31.338 --> 00:14:32.540
This is my home.

170
00:14:32.574 --> 00:14:33.541
Where am I supposed to go?

171
00:14:33.575 --> 00:14:35.175
My kids are in school.

172
00:14:35.209 --> 00:14:36.578
Why can't you
just arrest him now.

173
00:14:36.611 --> 00:14:37.645
you have this video?

174
00:14:37.679 --> 00:14:38.813
No arrest
can be made at this time.

175
00:14:38.847 --> 00:14:41.048
but I guarantee you.
we are monitoring him.

176
00:14:41.081 --> 00:14:44.318
What is important is that you
and your children find

177
00:14:44.351 --> 00:14:46.920
some place that you can stay
for a few weeks.

178
00:14:47.722 --> 00:14:49.557
This can't be happening.

179
00:14:49.591 --> 00:14:50.592
I'm not doing that.

180
00:14:52.126 --> 00:14:54.962
Why don't you and your kids
pack up some things

181
00:14:54.995 --> 00:14:57.665
and we will escort you
to the airport.

182
00:14:57.699 --> 00:14:59.133
You want us to leave right now?

183
00:14:59.166 --> 00:15:02.035
Ms. Davoudi. a credible threat
has been made upon your life.

184
00:15:02.069 --> 00:15:05.874
and I can guarantee
these guys do not wait around.

185
00:15:05.906 --> 00:15:08.342
I suggest you pack light.
you leave your phones

186
00:15:08.375 --> 00:15:11.513
and other electronic devices.
and you meet us outside.

187
00:15:11.546 --> 00:15:12.547
Detective.

188
00:15:18.553 --> 00:15:19.554
She had no idea.

189
00:15:21.288 --> 00:15:22.289
Didn't she?

190
00:15:25.492 --> 00:15:26.694
Mom. is everything okay?

191
00:15:29.764 --> 00:15:30.931
We have to leave.

192
00:15:30.964 --> 00:15:32.032
We have to leave now.

193
00:15:32.065 --> 00:15:33.868
I need you to pack a bag.
both of you.

194
00:15:33.902 --> 00:15:35.135
Okay. bring only what you need.

195
00:15:35.169 --> 00:15:38.038
-What did the police say?
-Why? What's going on?

196
00:15:38.071 --> 00:15:39.607
Just bring
some clothes for a week or two.

197
00:15:39.641 --> 00:15:40.742
Bring your school stuff.

198
00:15:40.775 --> 00:15:41.776
Don't forget your school stuff.

199
00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:42.976
Do not bring
your phones. actually.

200
00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:43.944
Leave your phones here.

201
00:15:43.977 --> 00:15:44.945
Look. you hear me?

202
00:15:44.978 --> 00:15:46.280
- You're scaring us.

203
00:15:46.313 --> 00:15:48.716
Look. please. just do as I say.
I will explain later.

204
00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:49.950
And hurry.

205
00:16:51.078 --> 00:16:52.714
Okay.
Here. give me those.

206
00:16:52.747 --> 00:16:53.815
Thank you. You guys get in.

207
00:16:53.848 --> 00:16:55.082
I got it.
-Thank you.

208
00:16:56.951 --> 00:16:58.786
Mom.

209
00:16:58.820 --> 00:17:00.087
you got to tell
us what's going on now.

210
00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.890
They think someone
wants to harm me.

211
00:17:01.923 --> 00:17:02.891
What?
Who?

212
00:17:02.924 --> 00:17:04.424
That's all I'm going to say.

213
00:17:04.458 --> 00:17:06.026
Mom. who?

214
00:17:06.961 --> 00:17:08.630
-Hey. is it Dad?
-I can't breathe.

215
00:17:08.663 --> 00:17:09.864
I can't breathe.
-Mom.

216
00:17:09.898 --> 00:17:11.198
-Hey. you're okay.
-It's okay.

217
00:17:11.231 --> 00:17:13.066
-You're okay.
-Please breathe with us.

218
00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:14.602
- You got to get in.

219
00:17:14.636 --> 00:17:15.469
Okay. yes.

220
00:17:15.503 --> 00:17:16.838
Mom. we got to go. Okay?
we got to go.

221
00:17:16.871 --> 00:17:17.605
Yes. go ahead.

222
00:17:17.639 --> 00:17:18.706
Come in.

223
00:17:19.473 --> 00:17:20.474
It's sorted.

224
00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:48.335
This is a burner phone.

225
00:17:48.368 --> 00:17:50.170
This is how we reach you
when you land.

226
00:17:50.203 --> 00:17:51.906
Keep it someplace safe.

227
00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:53.140
Where are we going?

228
00:17:53.741 --> 00:17:54.642
To a friend's.

229
00:17:55.810 --> 00:17:57.612
You said you had
a friend in Miami?

230
00:17:57.946 --> 00:17:58.980
Yes. I do.

231
00:17:59.013 --> 00:18:01.148
Call them
and we'll book you

232
00:18:01.181 --> 00:18:02.784
on the next flight out.

233
00:18:02.817 --> 00:18:05.085
And kids. don't call
your dad.

234
00:18:25.138 --> 00:18:27.775
- Darya. welcome to Miami.

235
00:18:27.809 --> 00:18:31.345
Oh. my God. I'm so glad
you had me so worried.

236
00:18:31.378 --> 00:18:33.915
Oh. you have no idea
how much this means to me

237
00:18:33.948 --> 00:18:35.349
and to all of us. really.

238
00:18:35.382 --> 00:18:36.951
It's always good
to see you. Dee.

239
00:18:36.985 --> 00:18:38.052
You. too.

240
00:18:38.086 --> 00:18:39.319
And you two.

241
00:18:40.253 --> 00:18:41.089
My God. you're getting
taller by the day.

242
00:18:41.121 --> 00:18:42.289
-Yes?
-Yes.

243
00:18:42.322 --> 00:18:44.025
Just wait till I get you
on the court.

244
00:18:44.058 --> 00:18:45.258
Challenge accepted.

245
00:18:46.094 --> 00:18:47.695
Look at this lovely lady.

246
00:18:49.964 --> 00:18:51.164
Hi.

247
00:18:54.636 --> 00:18:56.104
Okay. talk to me.

248
00:18:56.136 --> 00:18:57.337
What's going on?

249
00:18:58.238 --> 00:19:00.074
Later. Can we actually--

250
00:19:00.108 --> 00:19:01.809
Can we go up to the rooms?

251
00:19:01.843 --> 00:19:03.210
Yes. sure.

252
00:19:03.243 --> 00:19:05.412
We're already checked in.
so I got everything.

253
00:19:05.445 --> 00:19:06.848
Let's go.
Follow me.

254
00:19:06.881 --> 00:19:08.215
Come on. guys.

255
00:19:10.217 --> 00:19:11.719
All right. there we go.

256
00:19:15.222 --> 00:19:18.291
I don't understand.

257
00:19:19.827 --> 00:19:20.828
I don't believe it.

258
00:19:21.729 --> 00:19:23.865
The fact that he would want
to harm me

259
00:19:24.699 --> 00:19:25.967
or kill me.

260
00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:26.834
Really?

261
00:19:26.868 --> 00:19:28.235
The mother of his children.

262
00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:30.203
It doesn't feel real.

263
00:19:30.805 --> 00:19:31.806
